<title>DENMARK: Danish March yr/yr CPI up 1.5 pct (EU method).</title>
<headline>Danish March yr/yr CPI up 1.5 pct (EU method).</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish consumer prices were 0.1 percent higher in March 1997 from February 1997 and 1.5 percent up on March 1996, the National Statistics Office said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>    NEW EU FORMULA	     March 1997   Feb 1997  March 1996</p>
<p>    Change on month (pct)	+0.1	    0.0	+0.6</p>
<p>    Change on year (pct)	 +1.5	   +2.0	+1.7</p>
<p>    Index (base 1994)	    101.1	 101.0	99.6</p>
<p>NATIONAL FORMULA</p>
<p>    Change on month (pct)	 0.0	    0.0	+0.6</p>
<p>    Change on year (pct)	 +1.7	   +2.2	+2.1</p>
<p>    Index (base 1980)	    202.1	  202.0     198.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' average expectations were for a 2.1 percent yr/yr rise from March 1996 according to the national formula.</p>
<p>-- Chris Follett, Copenhagen Newsroom +45-33-969652</p>
</text>
